# --- deliberately NOT applied ----------------------------------------
# Listed here rather than merely omitted, so the next person can see the
# decision was made rather than forgotten.
#
# ingestion-source-medicare-pdf.sql
#     Registers a SYNTHETIC Medicare final rule — a PDF generated by
#     scripts/gen-medicare-test-pdf.mjs and served from our own
#     /test-fixtures/ — as an ACTIVE ingestion source, deliberately bound
#     to Traditional Medicare + OH "so rules actually persist", with
#     document_type 'cms_pfs', which carries a 0.95 confidence band and
#     writes created_by = 'crawler:cms_pfs' — the same marker the real
#     CY2026 Final Rule extraction uses. Its ON CONFLICT clause also
#     resets the fetch bookkeeping so the next cron tick re-extracts.
#     Applying it on a schedule would keep feeding invented Medicare
#     rules into the library 111 practices bill against. Run it by hand
#     against a test database, never from a deploy.
# 0016_phase11_design_partner_subscription.sql
#     Creates org 'Design Partner Co' with a fake Stripe subscription
#     (cus_DESIGN_PARTNER_DEV, status 'trialing'). Its own header says
#     production tenants get subscription rows from the Stripe webhook,
#     never from this seed. Applying it would put a synthetic tenant in
#     the client's org list. Dev and integration tests only.
# 0017_test_users.sql
#     Test accounts — never in production.
# 0018_test_palliative_payer_rules.sql
#     Fixture rules that would pollute the real library.
#
# The rule for adding to this manifest: if a seed writes to a tenant
# table (org, app_user, subscription, patient, visit, superbill,
# org_rulebook_row), it does not belong here. Reference data and the
# global rule library only.

